@startuml Kafka Data Flow

title Complete Data Flow - Write and Read Paths

actor Client

package "Write Path (Async)" {
    participant "FastAPI\n(Producer)" as API
    queue "Kafka Topic\n(3 partitions)" as Kafka
    participant "Consumer\nService" as Consumer
}

package "Read Path (Sync)" {
    participant "FastAPI\n(Query)" as QueryAPI
}

database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== Write Operations (CREATE/UPDATE/DELETE) ==

Client -> API: POST/PUT/DELETE\n{trade_data}
activate API

API -> API: 1. Validate Schema\n(Pydantic)

API -> API: 2. Build Message\n{operation, data}

API -> Kafka: 3. Produce Message\n(key=trade_id)
activate Kafka

Kafka -> Kafka: 4. Partition by Key\n(trade_id % 3)

Kafka --> API: 5. ACK
deactivate Kafka

API --> Client: 6. 202 Accepted\n(Queued)
deactivate API

...Async Processing...

Kafka -> Consumer: 7. Poll Message
activate Consumer

Consumer -> Consumer: 8. Parse & Validate

Consumer -> Consumer: 9. Route by Operation\n(CREATE/UPDATE/DELETE)

Consumer -> DB: 10. Execute\n(INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE)
activate DB

DB --> Consumer: 11. Success
deactivate DB

Consumer -> Kafka: 12. Commit Offset
activate Kafka
Kafka --> Consumer: ACK
deactivate Kafka

deactivate Consumer

== Read Operations (GET) ==

Client -> QueryAPI: GET /trades\nor /trades/{id}/{version}
activate QueryAPI

QueryAPI -> DB: SELECT Query
activate DB

DB --> QueryAPI: Result Set
deactivate DB

QueryAPI --> Client: 200 OK\n{trade_data}
deactivate QueryAPI

note right of Kafka
  **Message Format:**
  {
    "operation": "CREATE|UPDATE|DELETE",
    "data": {
      "trade_id": "T001",
      "version": 1,
      ...other fields...
    }
  }
  
  **Partitioning:**
  - Same trade_id → same partition
  - Preserves ordering per trade
  - Enables parallel processing
end note

note right of Consumer
  **Processing Guarantees:**
   At-least-once delivery
   Manual offset commits
   Ordered per partition
   Idempotent operations
   Error handling & retry
end note

note left of Client
  **API Responses:**
  
  Write Operations:
  → 202 Accepted (async)
  → 422 Validation Error (sync)
  → 503 Kafka Unavailable (sync)
  
  Read Operations:
  → 200 OK (sync)
  → 404 Not Found (sync)
end note

@enduml
